    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d920">

                <pb facs="0864" n="764" xml:id="pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.512/75</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 16.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to forward this enclosure for the
                    information of the Department.</p>
                <p>Although the present Turkish Government has no power of control over the local
                    Turkish authorities in the interior of Anatolia, it is considered proper to thus
                    register with the only recognized Turkish Government a protest against such
                    illegal taxation. I have informed all the Delegates of the United States High
                    Commissioner in Turkey and furnished them copies of this verbal note.</p>
                <p>If the Department desires to take any further action I request instructions.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mark L. Bristol</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d920-a1.xml" xpointer="d920-a1"/>
            </div>
